{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.fe7173df31","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-366","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1905.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Orla Observatory is in western Kenya. It began operating in 1926.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 8 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Pembrook Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Orla Observatory (8 meters).","The Pembrook Observatory began operating in 1905, while the Orla Observatory began operating in 1926.","The Pembrook Observatory, which is in southern New Zealand, is one of several radio observatories.","The Pembrook Observatory is in southern New Zealand, and the Orla Observatory is in western Kenya."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.20942c075a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-377","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Observatory is in northern Chile. It began operating in 1909.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 11 meters.</li><li>The Eastwick Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1963.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 2 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Observatory, which is in northern Chile, is one of several observatories located on remote mountaintops.","The Glenrock Observatory began operating in 1909, while the Eastwick Observatory began operating in 1963.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Glenrock Observatory (11 meters) is greater than that of the Eastwick Observatory (2 meters).","The Glenrock Observatory is in northern Chile, and the Eastwick Observatory is in southern New Zealand."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7441f93e90","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-380","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Orla Observatory is in northern India. It began operating in 1966.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Cresthill Observatory is in eastern Australia. It began operating in 2010.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 7 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Orla Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Cresthill Observatory (7 meters).","The Orla Observatory is in northern India, and the Cresthill Observatory is in eastern Australia.","The Orla Observatory, which is in northern India, is one of several radio observatories.","The Orla Observatory began operating in 1966, while the Cresthill Observatory began operating in 2010."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.591ab6e1ab","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-387","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Alder Museum is in eastern Australia. It opened in 1919.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 652,421 visitors.</li><li>The Quarry Museum is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 1964.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 602,601 visitors.</li><li>Both are art museums with free admission.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Alder Museum, which is in eastern Australia, is one of several art museums with free admission.","The Alder Museum opened in 1919, while the Quarry Museum opened in 1964.","The annual attendance of the Alder Museum (652,421 visitors) is greater than that of the Quarry Museum (602,601 visitors).","The Alder Museum is in eastern Australia, and the Quarry Museum is in southern New Zealand."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1d9ea42dc7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-388","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Umber Tunnel is in central Canada. It opened in 2015.</li><li>Its length is 21 kilometers.</li><li>The Ironwood Tunnel is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 1894.</li><li>Its length is 17 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Umber Tunnel, which is in central Canada, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The Umber Tunnel opened in 2015, while the Ironwood Tunnel opened in 1894.","The length of the Umber Tunnel (21 kilometers) is greater than that of the Ironwood Tunnel (17 kilometers).","The Umber Tunnel is in central Canada, and the Ironwood Tunnel is in southern New Zealand."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.55cac439b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-392","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tower is in western Kenya. It was completed in 2018.</li><li>Its height is 488 meters.</li><li>The Quarry Tower is in eastern Poland. It was completed in 1922.</li><li>Its height is 101 meters.</li><li>Both are towers built mainly of steel.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two towers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Tower is in western Kenya, and the Quarry Tower is in eastern Poland.","The Glenrock Tower was completed in 2018, while the Quarry Tower was completed in 1922.","The Glenrock Tower, which is in western Kenya, is one of several towers built mainly of steel.","The height of the Glenrock Tower (488 meters) is greater than that of the Quarry Tower (101 meters)."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8799c0f0a6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-0","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Adeyemi is a marine biologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Adeyemi recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Adeyemi found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Adeyemi found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Adeyemi concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","To investigate the question, Adeyemi recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Because whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often, Adeyemi concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.24f9707a98","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-8","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Sato is an ecologist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Sato compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Sato found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Sato concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Sato found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Because robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier, Sato concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","To investigate the question, Sato compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7cf668f9b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-23","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Nakamura is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","To investigate the question, Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.458a55773a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-25","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Takeda is a materials scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer, Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Takeda coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Takeda found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Takeda concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.192b87d6ee","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-41","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is a sociologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Varga surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Varga found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Varga concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Because residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened, Varga concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","To investigate the question, Varga surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Varga concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a4b306ce26","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-67","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Petrov is a linguist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Petrov gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Petrov found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Petrov concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Petrov gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Petrov found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","Petrov concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Because bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors, Petrov concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c995893e05","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-84","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Rahman is an urban planner.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Rahman measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Rahman found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Rahman concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Rahman measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Rahman found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Rahman concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Because streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler, Rahman concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.9c344838d3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-85","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Oyelaran is an urban planner.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Because streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler, Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.6456ad25a2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-99","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Castellano is an education researcher.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Castellano had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Castellano found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Castellano concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because children in the read-aloud group learned more new words, Castellano concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","To investigate the question, Castellano had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Castellano found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Castellano concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.079a8d8597","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-100","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Sato is an education researcher.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","To investigate the question, Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Because children in the read-aloud group learned more new words, Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.fbd8fead5a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-102","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Mbeki is a chemist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","To investigate the question, Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Because most samples broke apart within four months, Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1ec650ebda","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-118","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7568c6eba2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-129","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.17bd147a3a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-132","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Okafor is an archaeologist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Okafor analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Okafor found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Okafor concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Okafor found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","Okafor concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","To investigate the question, Okafor analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Because many pots were made from clay found only far inland, Okafor concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.621d70e8f3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-140","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Novak is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Because regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger, Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","To investigate the question, Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7e5104b6c7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-148","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Ferreira is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","To investigate the question, Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1db08558ce","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-151","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Duarte is a climate scientist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Duarte compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Duarte found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Duarte concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Duarte compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Duarte concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Duarte found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Duarte concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.79fdf95bb4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-155","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Okafor is a climate scientist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Okafor compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Okafor found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Okafor concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Okafor concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Okafor concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Okafor compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Okafor found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0c33f1a15b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-160","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Asante is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Because fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays, Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","To investigate the question, Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
